From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:07:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 49/76] flashnext: split DeltaNet prompt chain over (value
 head, slice) where the SMs allow

fn_gdn_chain_split steps each value head's 128 state rows in two blocks of
64 (eight threads a row, tree<8> keeps warp_sum's order), with the two cache
marks' states; fused passes take fn_gdn_front, the split chain and
fn_gdn_norm when every block has its own SM (96 SMs whole heads, 48 a rank's).
Registered as a replacement of fn_gdn_chain_tpr with two planted controls.
