diff --git a/docs/kernel-contract.md b/docs/kernel-contract.md
index 92dee9392..2e6a2e2ab 100644
--- a/docs/kernel-contract.md
+++ b/docs/kernel-contract.md
@@ -592,3 +592,10 @@ Only unsplit prompt calls select K32; fused slices retain the parent K64 tile.
 Each new control launches K32 for its output type at small and production row counts.
 `qmmf-prompt-bench` times the 64-row lane, prompt16, the parent K64 tile and K32 on each Flash Next BF16 shape.
 Measured nvcc 13.0 resources cover both K32 entries on sm_120 and sm_121; later compiler receipts remain pending.
+
+Flash Next's split prompt chain `fn_gdn_chain_split` (and `_h8`) steps each value head's 128 state rows in two blocks
+of 64, eight threads a row; the fused block's passes take it with `fn_gdn_front` and `fn_gdn_norm` where every block
+has an SM of its own (96 SMs for the whole layer's heads, 48 for a rank's). Its registration replaces
+`fn_gdn_chain_tpr`: ys, the state and two cache marks' states must equal its bytes. `flashnext-gdn-split-contract`
+runs both forms and two controls, red at gate 3: the launch one slice short, and each slice reading its neighbour's
+state. Its launches are in `flashnext_split_records.zig`, nvcc 13.0's usage; later compiler receipts remain pending.
